# Build context is the repo root (see docker/Dockerfile). Keep this narrow:
# it only trims things Docker never needs to COPY, not a general-purpose
# gitignore. Patterns are anchored to the repo root with a leading "/" where
# a bare name would otherwise also match same-named paths nested under
# backend/ or frontend/ (e.g. "docs" must not eat backend/assets/... — there
# is none today, but anchoring keeps that true by construction). The one
# deliberate exception is backend/assets/, which the runtime image needs
# (fonts) and which must survive every pattern below, including *.md.

.git

# Frontend: rebuilt fresh by the frontend-build stage; host artifacts (if
# any exist from local `npm run build`/`npm install`) would only bloat the
# context and can shadow stage output.
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist

# Backend: rebuilt fresh by the runtime stage's `uv sync`; a host .venv is
# almost certainly built for the host's arch, not the target image's.
backend/.venv
**/__pycache__
backend/.pytest_cache
backend/.ruff_cache

# Dev-only tooling (symbols_pipeline/'s fetch_*.py + regen_goldens.py):
# downloads/regenerates backend/assets/symbols/ and golden fixtures at dev
# time only. Nothing under backend/src/labelmaker/ imports it and no
# Dockerfile stage invokes it (grep docker/Dockerfile for "scripts" -- the
# only match is the frontend's unrelated scripts/copy-fonts.mjs, which lives
# under frontend/, not here), so it's pure dead weight in the shipped image.
# Distinct from backend/assets/, which the header note above already
# protects and which this pattern (anchored under backend/) can't touch.
backend/scripts

# Repo-local tooling, docs, and secrets that never belong in the image.
# .env is matched at ANY depth (not root-anchored like its neighbors):
# a docker/.env once sat inside the build context (context: ..) carrying a
# live API key -- review finding M8, docs/code-review-2026-08.md.
/.superpowers
/data
**/.env
/docs
/*.md
